__pycache__/
*.pyc
examples/scratch/
.pytest_cache/
# The forgeries are built, not published, with one exception. F5 is the record
# that passes every check in this repository and is still wrong, so it is the
# boundary section's claim as a runnable artefact rather than a sentence. A
# reader who runs the four that fail and never reaches the one that passes
# leaves thinking the format closes a gap it only names. It is tracked where
# forge.py writes it, not copied somewhere publishable, because a second copy
# of an artefact can drift from its generator; a test holds the tracked
# bytes against what forge.py reproduces. Its two registries come with it or
# it cannot be verified at all.
experiments/rederivability/out/*
!experiments/rederivability/out/f5-input-fabricated/
!experiments/rederivability/out/registry.json
!experiments/rederivability/out/deciders.json
